CallerPolicyValidationTest
├── when installing with empty callers array
│   └── it should revert with EmptyCallersArray
├── when installing with callers array containing zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddressCaller
├── when installing with valid callers array
│   ├── it should set status to Live
│   └── it should set allowedCaller for each caller
├── when reinstalling after uninstall with same policy id
│   ├── it should transition from Deprecated to Live
│   ├── it should reject the old caller
│   └── it should allow the new caller
├── when uninstalling with multiple and duplicate callers
│   ├── it should clear every caller using only the policy id
│   ├── it should reject signatures from all removed callers
│   └── it should reject a second uninstall with PolicyNotLive
├── when reinstalling while live
│   └── it should revert with PolicyAlreadyInstalled and preserve the current allowlist
├── when reinstalling with invalid callers
│   ├── it should reject empty lists and zero addresses
│   └── it should remain Deprecated without leaking partially installed callers
├── when reinstalling with other wallets and policy ids
│   └── it should preserve their independent allowlists
├── when rotating callers across repeated installations
│   └── it should allow only the current caller after each reinstall
├── when checking signature policy with sender as allowed caller
│   └── it should return validation success
├── when checking signature policy with sender not allowed
│   └── it should return validation failure
├── when checking signature policy for non installed account
│   └── it should return validation failure
├── when multiple callers are configured
│   ├── it should allow first caller
│   ├── it should allow second caller
│   └── it should reject non-configured caller
└── when caller is allowed for one account but not another
    ├── it should pass validation for allowed account
    └── it should fail validation for non-allowed account
